hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17360","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah twice, he said haddathana Abu al-Zara Amr ibn Amr, from his uncle Abi al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he looked me up and down and said: Are you owner of camels or owner of sheep. He said: From all, Allah has given me, much and good. He said: Then you produce them sound in eyes and ears, then you cut this and say: defective, then Sufyan spoke a word I did not understand, and you say: the Bahirah of Allah, for the arm of Allah is stronger and His blade sharper, and if He willed to bring it to you defective He would bring it. I said: To what do you call. He said: To Allah and to kinship. I said: A man from my cousins comes to me, so I swear not to give him, then I give him. He said: Expiate for your oath and do what is better. Have you seen, if you had two slaves, one obeys you and does not betray you nor lie to you, and the other betrays you and lies to you. He said: I said: No, rather the one who does not betray me nor lie to me and tells me truth is more beloved to me. He said: So likewise you are with your Lord, Exalted is He."
"17361","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi al-Ahwas, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a coarse wrap or two, so he said to me: Do you have wealth. I said: Yes, Allah, Exalted is He, has given me from all wealth, from His horses and camels and sheep and slaves. He said: When Allah gives you wealth, let His blessing be seen upon you. So I went to him in a fine suit."
"17362","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Sharik, then he mentioned it with its chain and meaning, he said: So I came to him in the morning in a red suit."
"17363","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, he said haddathana Sufyan, from Abi Ishaq, from Abi al-Ahwas, from his father Malik, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man I pass by and he does not host me nor entertain me, then he passes by me, shall I repay him. He said: No, rather host him. He said: Then he saw me shabby in appearance, so he said: Do you have wealth. I said: Allah, Exalted is He, has given me from all wealth, from camels and sheep. He said: Let the trace of the blessing of Allah be seen upon you."
"17364","Haddathana Ubaydah, he said haddathani Abu al-Zara, from Abi al-Ahwas, from his father Malik ibn Nadlah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hands are three: the hand of Allah the Highest, and the giving hand next to it, and the begging hand the lowest. So give the surplus and do not fail yourself."
